# Secrets for this Worker.
#
# The Deploy to Cloudflare button reads this file and asks for each value. It
# shows the names only, not these comments, so the guide a deployer actually
# reads is "What the two secrets are" in README.md — edit both together, or
# they drift. D1, R2, and the rate limiters are provisioned automatically from
# wrangler.jsonc and need nothing here.
#
# For local development, `bun run setup` applies migrations and prunes unused
# keys from .dev.vars.

# OpenRouter API key. This is what pays for every generated image, so put a
# spend limit on it: https://openrouter.ai/settings/keys
OPENROUTER_API_KEY=

# Mayar API key, used to sell credit packs. Payments are live: MAYAR_ENVIRONMENT
# is set to production in wrangler.jsonc, so this must be a production key from
# https://web.mayar.id/api-keys, not a sandbox one. To test with play money,
# set MAYAR_ENVIRONMENT=sandbox and use a key from https://web.mayar.io/api-keys.
MAYAR_API_KEY=

# BETTER_AUTH_SECRET is deliberately absent. The Worker generates it on first
# use and stores it in D1, so there is nothing to fill in. See ADR-0023.
#
# BETTER_AUTH_URL is absent for the same reason. It is optional, and the deploy
# button asks for every key listed here, so listing it made the form demand a
# value nobody can know before the deploy finishes. Set it as a secret
# afterwards. See "After the first deploy" in README.md.
